// fluxus_registratus.exsc -- UTF-8 to UTF-16 as a REGISTERED three-stage
// pipeline: each stage reads only what its predecessor latched on the previous
// tick and latches its own result.
//
// METHOD. Same three stages as fluxus_tres, now separated by registers, all
// fields of one `&mutabilis` struct (Registra), each a valid flag + payload:
//
//   input port -> stage 1 -> R1 -> stage 2 -> R2 -> stage 3 -> R3 -> output port
//
//   stage 1  gradus_primus    byte at the input pointer -> R1 (class, byte, its
//                             offset). State: Introitus (pointer, end-of-stream
//                             token issued).
//   stage 2  gradus_secundus  R1 -> R2: a scalar, or, for an ill-formed
//                             subpart, a halt (strict) or the scalar U+FFFD
//                             (substitue). State: Assemblatio. The mode is
//                             looked at here; fluxus_quattuor splits it out.
//   stage 3  gradus_tertius   R2 -> R3: a scalar becomes one or two UTF-16
//                             units, a halt passes through.
//   output   in converte      samples R3 after the tick's stages have run and
//                             appends its units to scopus. It is the observer
//                             of the last register, not a fourth stage.
//
// One pass of the loop in `converte` is one tick. The stages run in REVERSE
// order (3, 2, 1) so that each reads the register its predecessor has not yet
// overwritten. LATENCY IS 3 TICKS: a byte offered on tick t is in R1 after t,
// in R2 after t+1, in R3 after t+2, and the output port has it in scopus at the
// end of t+2. Measured: for every input that starts with an ASCII byte, the
// first unit is written on tick 3 (72,337 such inputs).
//
// FLUSH. The end of input is a token, not a side channel: once the bytes are
// spent stage 1 latches ONE item of class cl_finis, which stage 2 reads like
// any other item (a pending sequence becomes one ill-formed subpart), then
// stage 1 latches bubbles (valid flag 0). The loop runs until the token has
// been issued and R1, R2 and R3 are all empty. Measured on 543,648 inputs:
// ticks = n + r + 3, plus 1 more when the input ends inside a sequence (n = 0
// takes 2); r is the number of re-presented bytes below.
//
// THE RE-PRESENTED BYTE IS A STALL. When stage 2 refuses a byte (it breaks a
// pending sequence) it latches the result for the sequence into R2, goes idle,
// and raises `tene` for THIS tick. Stage 1 runs after stage 2 in the tick, so
// it sees `tene` already set, and does nothing at all: R1 keeps the refused
// byte, the valid flag stays 1, and the input pointer does not move. `tene` is
// the one signal here that is not a register: the refusal is discovered in the
// same tick in which stage 1 would otherwise overwrite R1, so a registered
// signal would arrive a tick too late. On the next tick stage 2 reads the same
// R1 with its state idle and takes the byte as the start of a new sequence;
// stage 1 resumes. Nothing is squashed and no bubble is inserted; each stall
// costs exactly one tick. Real trace for the bytes E2 41 42, substitue mode
// (values at the END of each tick; `tene` is the value stage 2 set that tick;
// "-" is an empty register; stage 2 reads the R1 of the previous line):
//
//   tick  tene  R1 (valid byte)  R2             R3             scopus gets
//    1     0    1 E2             -              -
//    2     0    1 41             -              -
//    3     1    1 41 (HELD)      FFFD           -
//    4     0    1 42             0041           FFFD           FFFD
//    5     0    1 EOS            0042           0041           0041
//    6     0    -                -              0042           0042
//    7     0    -                -              -
//
// Tick 3 is the stall: E2 was waiting for a continuation, 41 refused it, so
// R2 gets the replacement for E2 alone, R1 still holds 41, and stage 1 did not
// fetch 42. Tick 4 decodes the held 41 and only then fetches 42. In strict
// mode the same input latches a halt carrying offset 0 in R2 on tick 3, R3 on
// tick 4, where the output port returns.
//
// STRICT MODE. Stage 2 latches a halt carrying the sequence-start offset
// instead of a replacement. Nothing special drains the pipeline: the halt
// travels in order like any other item, so every item older than it is ahead
// of it, already written or in R3, and reaches the output port first. The
// output port acts on the halt only when it reaches R3; whatever is younger
// (in the trace above: R1 and the re-presented byte in R2) is dropped, never
// reaches scopus. So every unit before the error is emitted.
//
// WHERE THE MAXIMAL SUBPART COMES FROM. As in fluxus_tres: stage 2 accepts a
// continuation only if its class bit is set in `permissum` (Table 3-7 as a
// bit mask over the three continuation classes), and when a byte is refused,
// or the end-of-stream item arrives, the bytes assembled so far ARE the
// subpart. Its first byte is `inicium`, the offset stage 2 saved from R1 when
// it saw the lead; an ill-formed lead is its own subpart and uses R1's offset.
//
// NOT SHARED WITH ramus. No loop over fons[i + ate]; fons is read once per
// tick by stage 1, never looked ahead. The decoder state persists in structs
// across ticks, the three stages never run on the same item in the same tick,
// and a refused byte is re-offered by holding a register, not by re-reading
// the input. Shared because it is the standard: Table 3-7 and the surrogate
// arithmetic.

// ---- stage 1 vocabulary: the class of a byte -------------------------------

firma cl_ascii: u8 = 0;
firma cl_cont_a: u8 = 1;
firma cl_cont_b: u8 = 2;
firma cl_cont_c: u8 = 3;
firma cl_malus: u8 = 4;
firma cl_duo: u8 = 5;
firma cl_e0: u8 = 6;
firma cl_tres: u8 = 7;
firma cl_ed: u8 = 8;
firma cl_f0: u8 = 9;
firma cl_quattuor: u8 = 10;
firma cl_f4: u8 = 11;
firma cl_finis: u8 = 12;

// ---- what travels in R2 and R3 ---------------------------------------------

firma ev_scalaris: u8 = 1;
firma ev_halt: u8 = 2;

// Bit k of a `permissum` mask says: a byte of class k may be the next
// continuation. Classes 1, 2, 3 are the three continuation ranges.
firma perm_omnes: u32 = 14;
firma perm_e0: u32 = 8;
firma perm_ed: u32 = 6;
firma perm_f0: u32 = 12;
firma perm_f4: u32 = 2;

// The pipeline registers, one valid flag and one payload per register, plus
// `tene`, the single wire that is NOT a register (see gradus_secundus).
// A payload is meaningful only while its valid flag is 1.
structura Registra {
    v1: u8
    cl1: u8
    b1: u8
    off1: mensura
    v2: u8
    g2: u8
    cp2: u32
    pos2: mensura
    v3: u8
    g3: u8
    nu3: u8
    u0: u16
    u1: u16
    pos3: mensura
    tene: u8
}

// Stage 1's own state: the input pointer, and whether the end-of-stream token
// has been issued.
structura Introitus {
    p: mensura
    finis_missum: u8
}

// Stage 2's own state: the sequence being assembled.
structura Assemblatio {
    cp: u32
    opus: mensura
    permissum: u32
    inicium: mensura
}

// STAGE 1 logic. A byte in, a class out.
functio classis(b: u8) -> u8 {
    si b lt 0x80 {
        redde cl_ascii;
    }
    si b lt 0x90 {
        redde cl_cont_a;
    }
    si b lt 0xA0 {
        redde cl_cont_b;
    }
    si b lt 0xC0 {
        redde cl_cont_c;
    }
    si b lt 0xC2 {
        redde cl_malus;
    }
    si b lt 0xE0 {
        redde cl_duo;
    }
    si b eq 0xE0 {
        redde cl_e0;
    }
    si b eq 0xED {
        redde cl_ed;
    }
    si b lt 0xF0 {
        redde cl_tres;
    }
    si b eq 0xF0 {
        redde cl_f0;
    }
    si b lt 0xF4 {
        redde cl_quattuor;
    }
    si b eq 0xF4 {
        redde cl_f4;
    }
    redde cl_malus;
}

// STAGE 1. Reads the input port and its own pointer; latches R1. On a hold
// tick it does nothing at all: R1 keeps the byte stage 2 refused, and the
// pointer stays where it is.
functio gradus_primus(fons: acies<u8, 4096>, n: mensura, reg: &mutabilis Registra,
                      intro: &mutabilis Introitus) {
    si (*reg).tene eq 0 {
        si (*intro).p lt n {
            firma b: u8 = fons[(*intro).p];
            (*reg).v1 = 1;
            (*reg).cl1 = classis(b);
            (*reg).b1 = b;
            (*reg).off1 = (*intro).p;
            (*intro).p = (*intro).p + 1;
        } sin (*intro).finis_missum eq 0 {
            (*reg).v1 = 1;
            (*reg).cl1 = cl_finis;
            (*reg).b1 = 0;
            (*reg).off1 = n;
            (*intro).finis_missum = 1;
        } aliter {
            (*reg).v1 = 0;
        }
    }
}

// Stage 2's policy join: an ill-formed subpart starting at `pos` becomes a
// halt in strict mode and one U+FFFD in substitue mode. Latches R2.
functio mitte_malum(reg: &mutabilis Registra, modus: u8, pos: mensura) {
    (*reg).v2 = 1;
    si modus eq modus_stricte {
        (*reg).g2 = ev_halt;
        (*reg).pos2 = pos;
    } aliter {
        (*reg).g2 = ev_scalaris;
        (*reg).cp2 = 0xFFFD;
    }
}

// STAGE 2. Reads R1 (what stage 1 latched on the previous tick), its own
// state, and latches R2. It also drives `tene` for THIS tick: stage 1 runs
// after stage 2 in the tick, so it sees the value stage 2 just set.
functio gradus_secundus(reg: &mutabilis Registra, st: &mutabilis Assemblatio, modus: u8) {
    (*reg).tene = 0;
    (*reg).v2 = 0;
    si (*reg).v1 eq 0 {
        redde;
    }
    firma cl: u8 = (*reg).cl1;
    firma b: u8 = (*reg).b1;
    si (*st).opus gt 0 {
        si cl eq cl_finis {
            mitte_malum(reg, modus, (*st).inicium);
            (*st).opus = 0;
        } sin cl ge cl_cont_a et cl le cl_cont_c et (((*st).permissum deorsum (cl sicut u32)) atque 1) eq 1 {
            (*st).cp = ((*st).cp sursum 6) sive (b atque 0x3F) sicut u32;
            (*st).opus = (*st).opus - 1;
            (*st).permissum = perm_omnes;
            si (*st).opus eq 0 {
                (*reg).v2 = 1;
                (*reg).g2 = ev_scalaris;
                (*reg).cp2 = (*st).cp;
            }
        } aliter {
            mitte_malum(reg, modus, (*st).inicium);
            (*st).opus = 0;
            (*reg).tene = 1;
        }
        redde;
    }

    si cl eq cl_finis {
        redde;
    }
    si cl eq cl_ascii {
        (*reg).v2 = 1;
        (*reg).g2 = ev_scalaris;
        (*reg).cp2 = b sicut u32;
        redde;
    }
    mutabilis opus: mensura = 0;
    mutabilis masca: u8 = 0;
    mutabilis perm: u32 = perm_omnes;
    si cl eq cl_duo {
        opus = 1;
        masca = 0x1F;
    } sin cl eq cl_e0 {
        opus = 2;
        masca = 0x0F;
        perm = perm_e0;
    } sin cl eq cl_ed {
        opus = 2;
        masca = 0x0F;
        perm = perm_ed;
    } sin cl eq cl_tres {
        opus = 2;
        masca = 0x0F;
    } sin cl eq cl_f0 {
        opus = 3;
        masca = 0x07;
        perm = perm_f0;
    } sin cl eq cl_f4 {
        opus = 3;
        masca = 0x07;
        perm = perm_f4;
    } sin cl eq cl_quattuor {
        opus = 3;
        masca = 0x07;
    }
    si opus eq 0 {
        // a stray continuation or an ill-formed lead: one byte, consumed
        firma pos: mensura = (*reg).off1;
        mitte_malum(reg, modus, pos);
        redde;
    }
    (*st).opus = opus;
    (*st).cp = (b atque masca) sicut u32;
    (*st).permissum = perm;
    (*st).inicium = (*reg).off1;
}

// STAGE 3. Reads R2, latches R3: a scalar becomes one or two units, a halt is
// carried through untouched.
functio gradus_tertius(reg: &mutabilis Registra) {
    (*reg).v3 = 0;
    si (*reg).v2 eq 0 {
        redde;
    }
    (*reg).v3 = 1;
    si (*reg).g2 eq ev_halt {
        (*reg).g3 = ev_halt;
        (*reg).pos3 = (*reg).pos2;
        redde;
    }
    (*reg).g3 = ev_scalaris;
    firma cp: u32 = (*reg).cp2;
    si cp lt 0x10000 {
        (*reg).nu3 = 1;
        (*reg).u0 = cp sicut u16;
    } aliter {
        firma v: u32 = cp - 0x10000;
        (*reg).nu3 = 2;
        (*reg).u0 = (0xD800 + (v deorsum 10)) sicut u16;
        (*reg).u1 = (0xDC00 + (v atque 0x3FF)) sicut u16;
    }
}

publica functio converte(fons: acies<u8, 4096>, n: mensura,
                         scopus: &mutabilis acies<u16, 4096>, modus: u8) -> Exitus {
    mutabilis reg: Registra = Registra {
        v1: 0, cl1: 0, b1: 0, off1: 0,
        v2: 0, g2: 0, cp2: 0, pos2: 0,
        v3: 0, g3: 0, nu3: 0, u0: 0, u1: 0, pos3: 0,
        tene: 0
    };
    mutabilis intro: Introitus = Introitus { p: 0, finis_missum: 0 };
    mutabilis asm: Assemblatio = Assemblatio { cp: 0, opus: 0, permissum: perm_omnes, inicium: 0 };
    mutabilis j: mensura = 0;
    // One pass of this loop is one clock tick. Run until the input is spent,
    // the end-of-stream token has been issued and all three registers are empty.
    dum intro.finis_missum eq 0 vel reg.v1 eq 1 vel reg.v2 eq 1 vel reg.v3 eq 1 {
        // reverse order: each stage reads the register its predecessor
        // latched on the previous tick before the predecessor overwrites it
        gradus_tertius(reg);
        gradus_secundus(reg, asm, modus);
        gradus_primus(fons, n, reg, intro);
        // the output port: whatever stage 3 has just latched
        si reg.v3 eq 1 {
            si reg.g3 eq ev_halt {
                redde Exitus { unitates: j, status: status_malformatum, positio: reg.pos3 };
            }
            (*scopus)[j] = reg.u0;
            j = j + 1;
            si reg.nu3 eq 2 {
                (*scopus)[j] = reg.u1;
                j = j + 1;
            }
        }
    }
    redde Exitus { unitates: j, status: status_bene, positio: 0 };
}
